# Environment

Shell fences in rules and skills use POSIX syntax. If the session shell is PowerShell, translate syntax only. Never change the command, its flags, or its arguments.

In PowerShell on Windows, invoke `npm` and `npx` as `npm.cmd` and `npx.cmd`. This executable-name translation runs the same CLI without loading the `.ps1` launchers that execution policy can block. Keep the flags and arguments unchanged; do not change execution policy.

| POSIX | PowerShell |
|---|---|
| `VAR=value cmd` | `$env:VAR='value'; cmd` |
| `\` at line end | join into one line |
| `/tmp/name`, `$TMPDIR/name` | `$env:TEMP\name` |
| `name=$(cmd)` | `$name = cmd` |
| `a && b` | run `a`; run `b` only if `a` exited 0 (Windows PowerShell 5.1 has no `&&`) |
| `"<path>" args` | `& "<path>" args` |

Windows PowerShell 5.1 strips `"` embedded in an argument to a native program, such as `'{"a":1}'`. Use the owning file's quote-free form. If it has none, report the step as not run.

A POSIX-only tool with no PowerShell form in the owning rule or skill is not improvised. Report that step as not run.

In a multi-root workspace the Grep tool can search every root regardless of its `path` argument. When scope matters, search with shell `rg`, `grep`, or `git grep` against an explicit path or commit, and treat Grep tool matches outside the requested path as noise, not evidence.

Read executable paths from `AGENT_TOOLING_RUNTIME.tools`. Use the configured absolute paths, quoted when they contain spaces. A null or no-longer-runnable path is unavailable: stop only the operation requiring it and report it as not found or inaccessible, not necessarily uninstalled. A `ready` status means the workspace is configured; use `missingTools` and `warnings` for tool and role availability and remedies. Rerun `agent-tooling-setup` after installing or exposing tools; stale automatically discovered paths are refreshed using the configuration's `discoveredPaths` metadata. Manual overrides remain preserved even when inaccessible; correct these paths or set their configuration entries to null before setup to rediscover them. Do not guess a fallback or assume hook environment variables are inherited by shell commands.
